Fixes: f0e1a0643a59 ("sched_ext: Implement BPF extensible scheduler class")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # v6.12+
Reviewed-by: Andrea Righi <arighi@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Tejun Heo <tj@kernel.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug is a race condition where preemption occurs between the atomic claim of exit in scx_claim_exit() (which sets exit_kind and disables further error handling) and the subsequent kick of the helper kthread work (kthread_queue_work()). Once preempted, the task may not be rescheduled by the BPF scheduler (since error handling is disabled), so the helper work is never queued, bypass mode never activates, tasks stop being dispatched, and the system wedges.

Here is the patch:
